---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formatDate } from '../_posts.js';

// /opportunities/ -- three doors. The stack already exists and is free;
// these are the businesses it opens up. You bring the expertise.
//
// No prices, no "certified", no email addresses, no AI vendor named.
// Contact goes through the LinkedIn link. The Stripe data-pay anchors
// stay hidden exactly as they were. We never link jeyanandan.com from body.
const PUBLISHED = '2026-10-10';
const UPDATED = '2026-10-20';
const LINKEDIN = 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/jasonjeyanandan';
---
<Base
  title="Opportunities — Obsidian Delta"
  description="The MetaDAX stack already exists and is free: the recipe, the factory, the player, the showcases, the skills, the publishing system. These are the businesses it opens up — you bring the expertise, these are the tools.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">First published {formatDate(PUBLISHED)} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Updated {formatDate(UPDATED)}</p>
    <h1>Opportunities.</h1>
    <p class="deck">Everything below already exists, and all of it is free. These are the businesses it opens up: you bring the expertise, these are the tools.</p>
    <div class="rule"></div>
  </div></section>

  <div class="shell narrow">

    <!-- What already exists -- the stack, as solved problems -->
    <section class="plain" id="already-built" aria-labelledby="already-built-h2">
      <h2 id="already-built-h2">What already exists</h2>
      <ul class="built__list">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/metadax" rel="noopener">The open recipe</a> — the prompts that do the work live in <a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/metadax/tree/main/prompts" rel="noopener">prompts/</a>, free to read, copy and run.</li>
        <li><a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/grade-6-science-year/" rel="noopener">The factory</a> — one brief goes in and a whole course tree comes out, lessons, content and practice in order.</li>
        <li><a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/play/" rel="noopener">The player</a> — paste a package and it runs in the browser, nothing to install.</li>
        <li><a href="#showcase">The five showcases</a> — a French-fractions stadium, a staff onboarding module, a 3D biology lesson, a tutor's week, a whole Grade 6 science year.</li>
        <li><a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/" rel="noopener">The skills, in a plain chat</a> — homeschool, tutor, teacher, each a skill you run in an ordinary chat.</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/ObsidianDelta/published" rel="noopener">The publishing system</a> — everything versioned in the open, with the failures left in.</li>
        <li><a href="https://daxfoundation.org/definitions/#cognitive-companion" rel="noopener">The companion that builds it all</a> — a cognitive companion sits behind the factory and the skills, doing the building.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Coming: a cognitive companion of your own.</p>
      <p>On the frontier: retrieval over whole-course loading (X14), a dedicated safety path (X13), the once-a-day package, cultural packages, and the companion for you.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Door 1: Packages, built for you -->
    <section class="plain door" id="packages" aria-labelledby="door-packages">
      <p class="door__kicker">Door 1</p>
      <h2 id="door-packages">Packages, built for you</h2>
      <p>Meta DAX is free and open. Obsidian Delta builds the package you need on it, done for you, and you read it before it goes to a learner.</p>
      <p>The portfolio shows the shape: <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/tamil-chicken-curry/" rel="noopener">One dish, its story</a> (cultural knowledge, free to everyone who opens it); <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/words-into-algebra/" rel="noopener">Words into Algebra</a> (a tutor's hardest topic as a kit, with an Edition remade for one learner); <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/stockage-imbrique/" rel="noopener">Systèmes de fichiers imbriqués</a> (a French college module from one interview with the teacher); plus <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/first-week-at-the-bakery/" rel="noopener">First Week at the Bakery</a>, <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/grade-6-science-year/" rel="noopener">The Year on the Wall</a>, <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/proton-mill/" rel="noopener">The Proton Mill</a>, <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/tutors-desk/" rel="noopener">The Tutor's Desk</a>, <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/samples/stade-des-fractions/" rel="noopener">Le Stade des Fractions</a>, and the <a href="/opportunities/sample-report/">sample tutor report</a>.</p>
      <p>The same lesson, any skin, any language.</p>
      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="cta" data-pay="tutor-monthly" href="#" hidden>Pay with Stripe</a>
        <a class="cta" data-pay="tutor-single" href="#" hidden>Pay with Stripe</a>
        <a class="cta" data-cta="fallback" href={LINKEDIN} rel="noopener">Message Jason on LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Door 2: French editions -->
    <section class="plain door" id="french-editions" aria-labelledby="door-french">
      <p class="door__kicker">Door 2</p>
      <h2 id="door-french">French editions of your material</h2>
      <p>For teachers who sell their own resources: send one product and the first French edition comes back free. Canadian French, built from the editable source (PowerPoint, Slides or Canva), with the typography and the grade and curriculum labels a French-speaking teacher expects.</p>
      <p>Nothing of yours is used without your consent. The translation's copyright is yours.</p>
      <p>You check the content. French-speaking teachers who use it check the French.</p>
      <p>An interactive version in both languages is the next step up, built on the same kit as <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/showcases/words-into-algebra/" rel="noopener">Words into Algebra</a>.</p>
      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="cta" data-cta="french" href={LINKEDIN} rel="noopener">Message Jason on LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Door 3: Build with us -->
    <section class="plain door" id="build-with-us" aria-labelledby="door-build">
      <p class="door__kicker">Door 3</p>
      <h2 id="door-build">Build with us</h2>
      <p>Three ways in. Partners who want to run an initiative on the customer-management and content system Obsidian Delta runs its own work on: a team, Skippy doing the building, documents that stay inside the initiative. Contributors to the <a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/metadax" rel="noopener">open Meta DAX repository</a>. And a Meta DAX hackathon, open to everyone, where people build through that system without writing code — planned, with no date set yet.</p>
      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="cta" data-cta="build" href={LINKEDIN} rel="noopener">Message Jason on LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Who you're buying from -->
    <section class="plain" aria-labelledby="who">
      <h2 id="who">Who you're buying from</h2>
      <p>Obsidian Delta Corp, since 2017. The done-for-you builds above are the company's work. The DAX Foundation is the open project behind MetaDAX &mdash; separate, and not for sale.</p>
      <p class="free">The recipe is free at <a href="https://daxfoundation.org/metadax/" rel="noopener">daxfoundation.org/metadax/</a>. This page is for people who want to build something on it.</p>
      <p>Visits to this site are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics: no cookies, and no tracking of you from site to site.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>

<style is:global>
/* /opportunities/ in the Obsidian Delta dark system: white headings, bone body,
   orange as the single accent. Measures follow the blog (680px). Built on the
   same classes /learning/ used (.hero, .deck, .sc-*, .plain, .offer__price,
   .cta*, .free) with a small set added for the door kickers. */
.hero{padding:clamp(56px,10vw,96px) 0 clamp(28px,6vw,40px)}
.deck{
  font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;
  font-size:clamp(20px,3vw,26px);line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.01em;
  color:var(--ash);margin-top:16px;text-wrap:balance;
}

.plain{border-top:1px solid var(--steel);padding:clamp(32px,6vw,48px) 0}
.plain h2{
  font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:500;
  font-size:clamp(26px,3.8vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;
  color:var(--white);margin:0 0 .5em;text-wrap:balance;
}
.plain p{color:var(--bone);font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem;max-width:680px}
.plain p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.plain strong{color:var(--white);font-weight:500}
.plain a{color:var(--orange);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--orange)}
.plain a:hover{color:var(--white);border-color:var(--white)}
.free{color:var(--white)!important}

.built__list{list-style:none;margin:1.25rem 0 0;padding:0;max-width:680px}
.built__list li{
  color:var(--bone);font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;
  padding:0 0 .75rem 1.1rem;position:relative;
}
.built__list li:last-child{padding-bottom:0}
.built__list li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:.65em;width:6px;height:6px;background:var(--orange);border-radius:1px}
.built__list a{color:var(--orange);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--orange)}
.built__list a:hover{color:var(--white);border-color:var(--white)}

.door__kicker{
  font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;
  letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--orange);
  margin-bottom:10px!important;
}

.cta-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;margin:1.25rem 0 .5rem}
.cta{
  display:inline-block;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;
  letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--black)!important;background:var(--orange);
  padding:12px 22px;border:1px solid var(--orange)!important;border-radius:2px;
  text-decoration:none!important;transition:background .2s,color .2s;
}
.cta:hover{background:transparent;color:var(--orange)!important}
.cta[hidden]{display:none!important}
</style>
